# AWS EKS – Nginx Application Deployment

## Complete Command Reference

**AWS Region:** ap-south-1 (Mumbai)
**EKS Cluster:** eks-cluster
**EC2 Admin Instance:** Ubuntu
**Tools:** AWS CLI, eksctl, kubectl

---

## 1. Verify AWS Configuration

```bash
export AWS_PAGER=""
aws sts get-caller-identity
aws configure get region
aws eks list-clusters --region ap-south-1
```

## 2. Check EKS Cluster

```bash
aws eks describe-cluster --name eks-cluster --region ap-south-1 --query "cluster.status" --output text

aws eks update-kubeconfig --region ap-south-1 --name eks-cluster

kubectl get nodes
```

## 3. Check Existing EKS Access Entries

```bash
aws eks list-access-entries --cluster-name eks-cluster --region ap-south-1

aws eks describe-access-entry --cluster-name eks-cluster --principal-arn arn:aws:iam::053108159501:role/AmazonEKSAutoNodeRole --region ap-south-1
```

## 4. Create EKS Administrator IAM Role

```bash
aws iam create-role --role-name EKSClusterAdminRole --assume-role-policy-document '{"Version":"2012-10-17","Statement":[{"Effect":"Allow","Principal":{"AWS":"arn:aws:iam::053108159501:role/AmazonEKSAutoNodeRole"},"Action":"sts:AssumeRole"}]}'
```

Create EKS access entry:

```bash
aws eks create-access-entry --cluster-name eks-cluster --principal-arn arn:aws:iam::053108159501:role/EKSClusterAdminRole --type STANDARD --region ap-south-1
```

Associate cluster administrator policy:

```bash
aws eks associate-access-policy --cluster-name eks-cluster --principal-arn arn:aws:iam::053108159501:role/EKSClusterAdminRole --policy-arn arn:aws:eks::aws:cluster-access-policy/AmazonEKSClusterAdminPolicy --access-scope type=cluster --region ap-south-1
```

## 5. Assume Administrator Role

```bash
read -r AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY AWS_SESSION_TOKEN <<< "$(aws sts assume-role --role-arn arn:aws:iam::053108159501:role/EKSClusterAdminRole --role-session-name eks-admin --query 'Credentials.[AccessKeyId,SecretAccessKey,SessionToken]' --output text)" && export AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY AWS_SESSION_TOKEN
```

Verify:

```bash
aws sts get-caller-identity
kubectl get nodes
```

## 6. Deploy Nginx Application

Create deployment:

```bash
kubectl create deployment nginx --image=nginx
```

Check deployment:

```bash
kubectl get deployments
kubectl get pods
```

Expose Nginx using LoadBalancer:

```bash
kubectl expose deployment nginx --type=LoadBalancer --port=80 --target-port=80
```

Check service:

```bash
kubectl get svc nginx
```

## 7. Troubleshoot AWS LoadBalancer

Check service details:

```bash
kubectl describe svc nginx
```

Check service YAML:

```bash
kubectl get svc nginx -o yaml
```

Check cluster configuration:

```bash
aws eks describe-cluster --name eks-cluster --region ap-south-1 --query 'cluster.{ClusterRole:roleArn,ComputeConfig:computeConfig,Version:version}' --output json
```

Check Auto Mode load balancing:

```bash
aws eks describe-cluster --name eks-cluster --region ap-south-1 --query 'cluster.kubernetesNetworkConfig.elasticLoadBalancing' --output json
```

Check cluster IAM policies:

```bash
aws iam list-attached-role-policies --role-name AmazonEKSAutoClusterRole
```

## 8. Configure Public Subnet Tags

Switch back to EC2 instance role:

```bash
unset AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY AWS_SESSION_TOKEN
```

Verify identity:

```bash
aws sts get-caller-identity
```

Check subnet configuration:

```bash
aws ec2 describe-subnets --subnet-ids subnet-03605579ecd5bd571 subnet-0207457906e3c002d subnet-08223727a1f518148 --region ap-south-1 --query 'Subnets[].{SubnetId:SubnetId,AZ:AvailabilityZone,AvailableIPs:AvailableIpAddressCount,Tags:Tags}' --output json
```

Add public load balancer tags:

```bash
aws ec2 create-tags --resources subnet-03605579ecd5bd571 subnet-0207457906e3c002d subnet-08223727a1f518148 --tags Key=kubernetes.io/role/elb,Value=1 --region ap-south-1
```

Verify tags:

```bash
aws ec2 describe-subnets --subnet-ids subnet-03605579ecd5bd571 subnet-0207457906e3c002d subnet-08223727a1f518148 --region ap-south-1 --query 'Subnets[].{SubnetId:SubnetId,Tags:Tags}' --output json
```

## 9. Configure Public Network LoadBalancer

Switch to administrator role again:

```bash
read -r AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY AWS_SESSION_TOKEN <<< "$(aws sts assume-role --role-arn arn:aws:iam::053108159501:role/EKSClusterAdminRole --role-session-name eks-admin --query 'Credentials.[AccessKeyId,SecretAccessKey,SessionToken]' --output text)" && export AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY AWS_SESSION_TOKEN
```

Set the load balancer scheme:

```bash
kubectl annotate service nginx service.beta.kubernetes.io/aws-load-balancer-scheme=internet-facing --overwrite
```

Check service:

```bash
kubectl describe svc nginx
```

Watch for external hostname:

```bash
kubectl get svc nginx -w
```

## 10. Access Nginx Externally

Get the external hostname:

```bash
kubectl get svc nginx
```

Open the following URL in your browser:

```text
http://<EXTERNAL-IP>
```

Expected result:

**Welcome to nginx!**

